  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Customers pay for solving a real problem reliably. They judge you by delivery, honesty and follow-up.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is talking to ten possible customers before building anything.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and entrepreneurial skills: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft plans and messages. Routine planning shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Customer judgment, honest numbers and resilience hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and challenge your plan; later, own the decisions and the people.
  </p>

